---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const pageTitle = "Consulting";
---

<BaseLayout pageTitle={pageTitle}>
  <p>
    My consulting work is hands‑on, collaborative, and focused on building
    systems that feel fast, stable, and easy to work with. Whether you're
    dealing with performance issues, architectural uncertainty, or a roadmap
    that feels harder than it should, I work alongside your team to diagnose the
    real problems and guide you toward practical, long‑lasting solutions.
  </p>
  <h2>What I Do</h2>
  <p>
    Every team hits moments where the product feels slower, the architecture
    feels heavier, or the roadmap feels harder to execute than it should. I help
    teams cut through that complexity. My work focuses on diagnosing the real
    issues behind performance, reliability, and delivery friction — and guiding
    teams toward solutions that are clear, maintainable, and built to last.
  </p>
  <h3>Performance Optimization & Technical Diagnostics</h3>
  <p>
    Modern products slow down for all kinds of reasons — hidden bottlenecks,
    architectural drift, or small decisions that compound over time. I help
    teams uncover the real causes behind performance issues and fix them with
    clarity and precision. You get faster load times, smoother interactions, and
    a system that feels reliable instead of fragile.
  </p>
  <p>
    Typical outcomes:
    <ul>
      <li>Faster, more responsive user experience</li>
      <li>Reduced crashes and error rates</li>
      <li>Clear visibility into what's slowing you down</li>
      <li>Practical fixes that don't create new debt</li>
    </ul>
  </p>
  <h3>Software Reliability & Scalability Improvements</h3>
  <p>
    As your product grows, reliability becomes just as important as features. I
    help teams strengthen their systems so they can handle more users, more
    data, and more complexity without breaking. This is about building
    confidence — knowing your product can scale without surprises.
  </p>
  <p>
    Typical outcomes:
    <ul>
      <li>Fewer production incidents</li>
      <li>More predictable behavior under load</li>
      <li>Cleaner architecture that supports growth</li>
      <li>Reduced operational risk for the team</li>
    </ul>
  </p>
  <h3>Release Engineering & Workflow Improvements</h3>
  <p>
    Shipping should feel smooth, not stressful. I work with teams to improve
    their build pipelines, release processes, and development workflows so they
    can move faster with less friction. The goal is simple: make it easier for
    your team to deliver great work without fighting the tools.
  </p>
  <p>
    Typical outcomes:
    <ul>
      <li>Faster, more reliable deployments</li>
      <li>Reduced build times and CI/CD issues</li>
      <li>Clearer processes that unblock developers</li>
      <li>A calmer, more predictable release cycle</li>
    </ul>
  </p>
  <h3>Feature Development with Architectural Clarity</h3>
  <p>
    Sometimes you need to ship new features, but you don't want to create a mess
    that slows you down later. I help teams design and build features that fit
    cleanly into the existing system — or reshape the system when needed. You
    get progress without the hidden cost.
  </p>
  <p>
    Typical outcomes:
    <ul>
      <li>Features that are maintainable from day one</li>
      <li>Cleaner, more intentional code</li>
      <li>Reduced future refactoring</li>
      <li>A product that evolves without accumulating chaos</li>
    </ul>
  </p>
  <h2>Who I Work With</h2>
  <p>
    I partner with teams who care about clarity, quality, and long‑term
    maintainability. Most of my clients fall into one of these groups:
    <ul>
      <li>
        <b>Product teams shipping complex React/Node.js applications</b>
        Teams that need help diagnosing performance issues, improving reliability,
        or making architectural decisions with confidence.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Creative tool builders</b>
        Founders and teams working on graphics-heavy, real‑time, or generative tools
        who need support with performance, rendering pipelines, or UX clarity.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Early-stage startups</b>
        Companies moving fast but starting to feel the weight of technical debt, unclear
        architecture, or slow delivery cycles.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Teams struggling with performance or reliability issues</b>
        Products that feel slower than they should, systems that break under load,
        or codebases that have become harder to evolve.
      </li>
      <li>
        <b>Engineering teams that want a trusted technical advisor</b>
        Leads and founders who want a clear, experienced voice to help them make better
        technical decisions and avoid costly mistakes.
      </li>
    </ul>
    If your team values thoughtful engineering, clear communication, and practical
    solutions, we'll work well together.
  </p>
  <h2>How I Work</h2>
  <p>
    Working with me is straightforward and intentionally lightweight. My goal is
    to bring clarity, momentum, and technical confidence to your team without
    adding overhead or complexity.
    <ol>
      <li>
        <b>Fit Call</b>
        A short conversation to understand your challenges, your goals, and whether
        I'm the right person to help. If I'm not, I'll point you in the right direction.
      </li><li>
        <b>Deep Dive</b>
        If we're a match, we start with a focused exploration of your codebase, architecture,
        and workflows. This gives me the context I need to identify the real issues
        behind performance, reliability, or delivery friction.
      </li><li>
        <b>Engagement</b>
        Depending on your needs, this can be weekly advisory, a targeted audit, or
        a short project. I work closely with your team, offering clear guidance, hands‑on
        support, and practical solutions that fit your roadmap.
      </li><li>
        <b>Ongoing Support or Handoff</b>
        Once the core work is done, I either stay on as a technical sounding board
        or hand everything off with clear next steps. The goal is always the same:
        leave your team stronger and more confident than before.
      </li>
    </ol>
    This process keeps things simple, predictable, and focused on outcomes — not busywork.
  </p>
  <h2>Book a Fit Call</h2>
  <p>
    If this sounds like the kind of support your team needs, I'd love to learn
    more about what you're building. A fit call is a short, friendly
    conversation where we explore your challenges, your goals, and whether I'm
    the right person to help. No pressure, no hard sell — just clarity.
    <br /><b>Let's see if we're a good match.</b>
    <br /><em>Book a fit call and we'll take it from there.</em>
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
